verifyExecution.t.sol
└── when caller is not whitelisted
│   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedSource
└── when caller is whitelisted
    ├── when mode is SmartSession.USE
    │   ├── when permissionId is not enabled
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidPermissionId
    │   ├── when permissionId is enabled
    │   │   ├── when selector is not execute
    │   │   │   └── it should revert with UnsupportedSelector
    │   │   ├── when selector is execute
    │   │   │   ├── when execution type is not DEFAULT
    │   │   │   │   └── it should revert with UnsupportedExecutionType
    │   │   │   ├── when execution type is DEFAULT
    │   │   │   │   ├── when call type is SINGLE
    │   │   │   │   │   ├── when action policy check passes
    │   │   │   │   │   │   ├── when signature is valid
    │   │   │   │   │   │   │   └── it should return verifyExecution.selector
    │   │   │   │   │   │   └── when signature is invalid
    │   │   │   │   │   │       └── it should return 0xFFFFFFFF
    │   │   │   │   │   └── when action policy check fails
    │   │   │   │   │       └── it should revert
    │   │   │   │   └── when call type is BATCH
    │   │   │   │       ├── when action policy check passes
    │   │   │   │       │   ├── when signature is valid
    │   │   │   │       │   │   └── it should return verifyExecution.selector
    │   │   │   │       │   └── when signature is invalid
    │   │   │   │       │       └── it should return 0xFFFFFFFF
    │   │   │   │       └── when action policy check fails
    │   │   │   │           └── it should revert
    │   │   │   └── when call type is not supported (e.g., DELEGATECALL)
    │   │   │       └── it should revert with UnsupportedExecutionType
    └── when mode is SmartSession.ENABLE
        ├── when enable signature is invalid
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidEnableSignature
        ├── when enable signature is valid
        │   ├── when ISessionValidator is not already set
        │   │   └── it should enable ISessionValidator and check policies
        │   │       ├── when signature is valid
        │   │       │   └── it should return verifyExecution.selector
        │   │       └── when signature is invalid
        │   │           └── it should return 0xFFFFFFFF
        │   └── when ISessionValidator is already set
        │       └── it should just add policies and check them
        │           ├── when signature is valid
        │           │   └── it should return verifyExecution.selector
        │           └── when signature is invalid
        │               └── it should return 0xFFFFFFFF
    └── when mode is unsupported
        └── it should revert with UnsupportedSmartSessionMode